      "text": "The arrows show \n\ud835\udc42\n\ud835\udc34\n\u2192\n=\n\ud835\udc4e\n, \n\ud835\udc42\n\ud835\udc35\n\u2192\n=\n\ud835\udc4f\n, and \n\ud835\udc42\n\ud835\udc36\n\u2192\n=\n\ud835\udc50\n. Solid grid lines are one unit apart; dotted lines divide each square in half.\n\nGiven that \n\ud835\udc50\n=\n\ud835\udf06\n\ud835\udc4e\n+\n1\n2\n\ud835\udc4f\n, find \n\ud835\udf06\n.\n\n\ud835\udf06\n=\n \n.\n\nCORRECT\nPreview only\nSolution:\n\nAnswer 1 \u00b7 correct value:\n\n3\n2\n\nConstruct the known component \n1\n2\n\ud835\udc4f\n from \n\ud835\udc42\n, and call its endpoint \n\ud835\udc43\n. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:\n\n\ud835\udc42\n\ud835\udc43\n\u2192\n\t\n=\n1\n2\n(\n2\n,\n\u2212\n3\n)\n=\n(\n1\n,\n\u2212\n3\n2\n)\n.\n\n\n\ud835\udc43\n\ud835\udc36\n\u2192\n\t\n=\n(\n3\n,\n\u2212\n6\n)\n.\n\nCompare the remaining displacement with \n\ud835\udc4e\n, whose grid displacement is \n(\n2\n,\n\u2212\n4\n)\n:\n\nHorizontal scale\n\t\n=\n3\n2\n=\n3\n2\n\n\nVertical scale\n\t\n=\n\u2212\n6\n\u2212\n4\n=\n3\n2\n\nThe scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as \n\ud835\udc4e\n. Thus \n\ud835\udc43\n\ud835\udc36\n\u2192\n=\n3\n2\n\ud835\udc4e\n. By the triangle law,\n\n\ud835\udc50\n\t\n=\n\ud835\udc42\n\ud835\udc43\n\u2192\n+\n\ud835\udc43\n\ud835\udc36\n\u2192\n\n\t\n=\n1\n2\n\ud835\udc4f\n+\n3\n2\n\ud835\udc4e\n\n\t\n=\n3\n2\n\ud835\udc4e\n+\n1\n2\n\ud835\udc4f\n.\n\nThe vectors \n\ud835\udc4e\n and \n\ud835\udc4f\n are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of \n\ud835\udc4e\n gives \n\ud835\udf06\n=\n3\n2\n.\n\nBack to study \u2192",
